{"version":1,"slug":"Others__WORD_BASED_(1)","path":"Others/WORD BASED (1).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"WORD BASED (1).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A number has been denoted to each of the given letters. Select the combination of numbers so that the jumbled letters arranged accordingly will form a meaningful English word. The letters and their corresponding numbers are listed below:</p><p>A = 1, C = 2, G = 4, H = 8, I = 5, P = 3, R = 7, S = 6</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364;&#2368; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2375;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;:</p><p>A = 1, C = 2, G = 4, H = 8, I = 5, P = 3, R = 7, S = 6</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5,3,7,1,8,2,4,6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5,3,7,1,8,2,4,6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3,8,2,4,7,1,5,6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3,8,2,4,7,1,5,6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4,7,1,3,8,5,2,6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4,7,1,3,8,5,2,6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2,6,4,7,1,3,8,5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2,6,4,7,1,3,8,5</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>G(4), R(7), A(1), P(3), H(8), I(5), C(2), S(6) spells GRAPHICS.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Each of the letters in the word 'DIAMOND' is arranged in the English alphabetical order. How many letters are there in the English alphabetical series between the letter which is fourth from the left end and the one which is third from the right end in the new letter-cluster thus formed?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; 'DIAMOND' &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2344;&#2319; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;-&#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2331;&#2379;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2380;&#2341;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2331;&#2379;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Two</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2379;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Four</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Three</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2368;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">More than three</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Original: D I A M O N D</p><p>Sorted : A D D I M N O</p><p>The English alphabetical series between the letter which is fourth from the left end: I</p><p>The one which is third from the right end in the new letter-cluster thus formed: M</p><p>The alphabets are J, K and L. </p><p>Thus, three letters are there in the English alphabetical series between the letter which is fourth from the left end and the one which is third from the right end in the new letter-cluster thus formed. </p><p>So, option (c) is the correct answer. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Each of the letters in the word 'NATIONAL' is arranged in the English alphabetical order. Which letter comes immediately before T in the new letter-cluster thus formed?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>'NATIONAL' &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2344;&#2319; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;-&#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; T &#2360;&#2375; &#2336;&#2368;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">N</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">N</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">O</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">O</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">L</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">L</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">I</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Original: N A T I O N A L</p><p>Sorted : A A I L N N O T</p><p>Letter before T = O</p><p>So, option (b) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Given the letters T, M, A, E in random order, form all possible meaningful words. How many of those words end with a vowel?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; T, M, A, E &#2325;&#2379; &#2351;&#2366;&#2342;&#2371;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2352;, &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2325; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">One</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Two</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2379;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Three</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2368;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eq