s a scrap or remainder of food from a meal. </p><p>Total = 4 =&gt; option d</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many meaningful English words can be formed with the 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 6th letters of the word <b>FLAMES</b>, using each letter only once in each word?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; <b>FLAMES</b> &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375;, &#2330;&#2380;&#2341;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2331;&#2336;&#2375; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Zero</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">One</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Two</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2379;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Three</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2368;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Letters selected: L, A, M, S</p><p>Meaningful words: SLAM, LAMS, ALMS</p><p>SLAM means to shut (door, window or lid) forcefully and loudly. </p><p>LAMS means hit hard or strike. </p><p>ALMS means money, food and clothes given to poor people. </p><p>Total = 3 =&gt; option d</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}